## 1. Architecture Topology

### Component Locations

| Component | Platform | Resource Name | Region |
|---|---|---|---|
| LibreChat | Azure Container Apps | `librechat-nonprod` | `<AZURE_REGION>` |
| LiteLLM gateway | Azure Container Apps | `litellm-nonprod` | `<AZURE_REGION>` |
| LibreChat storage | Azure Files (SMB) | `<STORAGE_ACCOUNT>` | `<AZURE_REGION>` |
| LiteLLM config | Azure Files (read-only) | `<STORAGE_ACCOUNT>` | `<AZURE_REGION>` |
| Model deployments | Azure OpenAI / AI Foundry | `<AI_FOUNDRY_RESOURCE>` | `<AZURE_REGION>` |
| Authentication | Okta (external) | `romtech.okta.com` | n/a |

### Request Flow

```
Browser (Okta-authenticated user)
  │
  ▼ HTTPS (ACA ingress, port 3080)
LibreChat — Azure Container App
  │  reads: /app/api/data/librechat.yaml  (Azure File Share)
  │  writes: /app/api/data/*.sqlite        (Azure File Share)
  │
  ▼ HTTPS (virtual API key, /v1/chat/completions)
LiteLLM Gateway — Azure Container App
  │  reads: /app/config/litellm_config.yaml (Azure File Share, read-only)
  │  enforces: allowlist, rate limits, usage tracking
  │
  ▼ HTTPS (Azure OpenAI API key)
Azure OpenAI / AI Foundry
  ├── Flagship deployment (ROMTech AI Standard → <DEPLOYMENT_FLAGSHIP>)
  └── Fast deployment    (ROMTech AI Fast     → <DEPLOYMENT_FAST>)
```

### Model Configuration Location

Model names, routing targets, and allowlist enforcement are defined in
`litellm_config.yaml` on the Azure File Share mounted by the LiteLLM container.
Updating this file and restarting the LiteLLM container changes model availability
without a container redeployment.

