## 4. Gaps and Risks

All Phase 0 issues classified using the four-tier framework:
- **Acceptable for v1** — Minor gaps that do not violate security or data policy
- **Fix before v1** — Must be resolved before production deployment
- **Needs stakeholder decision** — Requires leadership authorization
- **Blocker** — Critical failure preventing deployment

| Identified Gap or Risk | Classification | Recommended Action |
|---|---|---|
| Temporary Azure OpenAI routing (PBI 9125) bypasses LiteLLM tracking | Fix before v1 | Completed in PBI 9126 — verify env vars removed |
| SQLite database has no HA (single Azure File Share, no replication) | Acceptable for v1 | Acceptable for POC scale; plan PostgreSQL migration for v2 |
| Okta group assignment requires external admin coordination | Needs stakeholder decision | Formalize cross-department SLA for user provisioning turnaround |
| Model name aliases depend on Dev 1 PBI-04-BE handoff | Fix before v1 | Completed — confirm final names in dev2_handoff.md |
| File upload and RAG disabled pending compliance review | Needs stakeholder decision | Define compliance review scope and timeline for a later phase |
| LiteLLM rate limiting requires PostgreSQL for reliable per-key enforcement | Needs stakeholder decision | Decide whether to provision PostgreSQL before v1 launch |
| <!-- Add any additional gaps found during Phase 0 --> | | |

