## 6. Backlog Handoff Parameters (v1 PBIs)

The following v1 PBIs are derived directly from Phase 0 findings and are ready to
be pulled into Sprint 1 upon leadership sign-off.

| PBI Title | Derived From | Priority | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Provision PostgreSQL for LiteLLM spend tracking and rate limiting | Rate limiting assessment (PBI-06-BE) | High | Required for per-user daily limits and monthly team caps |
| Configure per-department LiteLLM virtual keys with budget caps | Rate limiting assessment (PBI-06-BE) | High | One key per team/department with `max_budget` and `budget_duration` |
| Configure LiteLLM budget alert callbacks | Rate limiting assessment (PBI-06-BE) | Medium | Alerts at 75% and 90% of monthly cap |
| Switch LibreChat to PostgreSQL backend | Persistence findings (PBI 9128) | Medium | Required for HA and horizontal scaling in v1 |
| Complete Okta pilot group rollout | Okta validation (PBI 9129) | High | Coordinate with Okta admin; define provisioning SLA |
| Compliance review for file upload and RAG features | Feature audit (PBI 9130) | Medium | Define scope and timeline; unblock in a later phase if approved |
| Production image pinning and container hardening | Deployment (PBI 9125) | High | Pin to release tags; review container security posture |
| Azure Monitor integration for operational observability | Usage tracking (PBI-05-BE) | Medium | Forward LiteLLM spend logs to Azure Monitor / Log Analytics |

